      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "bundle/patches/kernel/0001-*",
        "bundle/patches/kernel/0002-*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HCAP-04",
      "name": "lane execution topology",
      "purpose": "Runtime selections this host executes; one proc on lane 0",
      "usable_stage": [
        "stage1"
      ],
      "usable_by": [
        "agent_stage1"
      ],
      "interface": {},
      "constraints": [
        "nfs.localio_enabled=N",
        "single fixture, koov.nfs_version from the selection",
        "nlm-knfsd fixture (koov.nfs_fixture=nlm-knfsd) for the NFSv3 HCAP-13 selection"
      ],
      "status": "partially_validated",
      "scope": [
        "one_lane"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "bundle/lane/boot-fixture.sh"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HCAP-11",
      "name": "bounded NFSv4.1 client lifecycle recovery",
      "purpose": "Expire the deterministic confirmed lane-0 client and drive protocol-valid NFSv4.1 recovery",
      "usable_stage": [
        "stage1"
      ],
      "usable_by": [
        "agent_stage1"
      ],
      "interface": {
        "syz_calls": [
          "syz_nfsd_client_ctl$expire_client0"
        ]
      },
      "constraints": [
        "single NFSv4.1 fixture with SERVER_IMPL=both and the lifecycle broker enabled",
        "client0 is the only admitted client selector; invoke exactly one syz_nfsd_client_ctl$expire_client0(0x0), acquire the client0 profile exactly once, then perform at least one parser-proven client0-origin NFS I/O operation",
        "broker resolves exactly one confirmed minor-version-1 owner named Linux NFSv4.1 frozen-phase9-lane0-client0/<UTS hostname>",
        "broker alone selects /proc/fs/nfsd/clients/<client>/ctl and writes literal expire",
        "validated recovery pairs one expiry with ordinary client0 profile I/O and observes EXCHANGE_ID then CREATE_SESSION"
      ],
      "status": "validated",
      "scope": [
        "client0_confirmed_expiry_recovery"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "bundle/patches/syzkaller/0027-*",
        "bundle/lane/lane.sh",
        "tools/nfs-proxy/src/lifecycle.c",
        "tools/nfs-lifecycle/run.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HCAP-12",
      "name": "bounded nfsdcld reconnect during NFSv4.1 client recovery",
      "purpose": "Replace the lane nfsdcld pipe reader while a recovered client0 records itself through the CLD upcall",
      "usable_stage": [
        "stage1"
      ],
      "usable_by": [
        "agent_stage1"
      ],
      "interface": {
        "syz_calls": [
          "syz_nfsd_cld_ctl$reconnect"
        ]
      },
      "constraints": [
        "single NFSv4.1 fixture with the lifecycle broker managing the lane nfsdcld",
        "within the HCAP-11 sequence invoke exactly one syz_nfsd_cld_ctl$reconnect(0x2) after syz_nfsd_client_ctl$expire_client0(0x0) and before the client0 profile acquisition; syz_nfsd_cld_ctl$daemon_down is never admitted",
        "the broker alone selects the daemon by namespace, start time, command, executable and owned rpc_pipefs CLD pipe, holds it stopped for a bounded time, then replaces it and refuses overlapping operations",
        "only nfsd request-context CLD work is attributed; daemon, rpciod and broker-process CLD work is remote_kcov.context.cld"
      ],
      "status": "validated",
      "scope": [
        "client0_recovery_cld_reconnect"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "bundle/patches/syzkaller/0028-*",
        "bundle/lane/lane.sh",
        "tools/nfs-proxy/src/cld.c",
        "tools/nfs-lifecycle/run.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HCAP-13",
      "name": "NLM lane locking and raw NLM RPC",
      "purpose": "Drive the lane knfsd lockd through kernel NFS client byte-range locks and raw NLM calls on the nlm-knfsd NFSv3 fixture",
      "usable_stage": [
        "stage1"
      ],
      "usable_by": [
        "agent_stage1"
      ],
      "interface": {
        "syz_calls": [
          "fcntl$lock",
          "recvfrom$inet_nlm_tcp",
          "syz_nlm_lane_fh",
          "syz_open_nlm_lane_file",
          "syz_send_nlm_rpc",
          "syz_socket_connect_nlm$client0",
          "syz_socket_connect_nlm$client1"
        ]
      },
      "constraints": [
        "nlm-knfsd fixture only: the single NFSv3 knfsd lane with SERVER_IMPL=both, rpcbind and rpc.statd in every lane namespace, both knfsd mounts locking and lockd on TCP port 4045",
        "lock files: r1 = syz_open_nlm_lane_file(r0, name, mode) beneath a knfsd-v3 lane fd (names lock0, lock1, lock2, shared/fixture; mode 0 read-only, 1 read-write, 2 read-write and create), then fcntl$lock(r1, 0x5 F_GETLK or 0x6 F_SETLK, flock); F_SETLKW and OFD locks are never admitted because the collector runs one non-threaded program",
        "raw NLM: r3 = syz_socket_connect_nlm$client0(0x0) or $client1(0x1), then syz_send_nlm_rpc(r3, rpc_nlm_call, len) with exact len fields; the @lane file handle takes r2 = syz_nlm_lane_fh(r0, name) of an existing lane file; read each reply with recvfrom$inet_nlm_tcp before the next call",
        "attributed: the server lane lockd serving a TCP NLM request and the client lane lockd serving a TCP callback; the server lockd thread granting a blocked lock, rpciod NLM callbacks and UDP NLM are remote_kcov.context.lockd"
      ],
      "status": "validated",
      "scope": [
        "nlm_lane_lock_rpc"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "bundle/patches/syzkaller/0030-*",
        "bundle/lane/lane.sh",
        "tools/nfs-lifecycle/run.py"
      ]
    }
  ],
